// Objective - DestroyerBoss 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P1679433941" "Take down the Destroyer Ring Leader"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3289273956" "You've learned a surprising secret - Praetor Duncan was the one behind the Destroyers all this time!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2275168248" "{HeroName}, what did you find?<br><br>Ohmygodwhat?! Praetor Duncan is the leader of the Destroyers? <i>She</i> was the one who was directing them all this time in Imperial? This is, wow, uhm, this is some crazy stuff, {HeroName}, crazy stuff! We always knew that outside of her public persona she was pretty twisted, but this is something else! Do you realize how <i>big</i> you're going to become, {HeroName}, once you reveal this to the public? Oh, this is going to be <i>huge</i>! I can see the headlines now, '{HeroName} reveals Praetor Duncan's operations, Cole debates making {HeroName} a new Praetor!'<br><br>We've gotta get on this and <i>fast</i>. Duncan is going to know that <i>we</i> know about her operations. There's no time to lose!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Reporter 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2748861679" "{HeroName}! John Houston, TPN, let me just say, it's an honor to see you here, ready to fight the TPN horde! We've got our cameras ready to roll. Just say the word! I, of course, will be up in our building, watching and commenting as you wade through the horde!"
// Answer Text :
"P2369758842" "Alright, start filming."
// Answer Text :
"P379013455" "Give me a second."
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P1658182072" "Alright, I'll give the word!"
// Answer Text :
"P4060782435" "Leave"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogDomi 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1302334636" "Well well, big bad {HeroName}. The {Hero.gender=male man|woman} responsible for crippling the Destroyers, for saving TPN, and revealing my dirty little secret. I have to give you credit, {HeroName}. I thought you were going to be <i>dumb</i> enough to try to put Praetor White down instead of investigating further. Just goes to show that I underestimated you."
// Answer Text :
"P1795085298" "Cole is still keeping you around, after all that?"
// Page InformationPage1 Text :
"P970081998" "<color orange>Praetor Duncan grins coyly.</color><br><br>When I explained how things <i>really</i> went, everything was fine. You see, {HeroName}, <color yellow>Praetor Keyes</color> was kind enough to reveal the truth of the matter, that <i>he</i> was the one who was this whole mess with the Destroyers. I, of course, was just an innocent bystander. Keyes was <i>so</i> willing to help me out of this little jam, you should've seen him!<br><br>Of course, I didn't get off so easily, little Marcus told me I couldn't play with my Destroyers anymore, so there goes that whole bit of fun. And Praetor White told me not to lay a hand on you, or else he'd get involved. Isn't that just awful?"
// Answer Text :
"P4291539279" "So you used Praetor Keyes to get yourself out of this situation."
// Page Used Text :
"P2394139804" "I did. Of course, you know the truth, don't you? That's why the people of Imperial love you now. But I know your type, {HeroName}. I know that you're not out to save the people here in Praetoria. I <i>know</i> that deep down inside, you look out for number one. It's why I can understand you. Hehe! We're both the same, you know. Just looking to get ourselves some fun and power. You did good today, but how many times have you hurt others to make yourself look good? I've done it plenty more times than you, trust me.<br><br>But at the end of the day, it's all about the image that the people have of you. If no one knows you killed twenty people to save one important person, who cares? Isn't that right? So don't try to act as if <i>I'm</i> the bad guy in this situation. You're just as <i>rotten</i> to the core as I am."
// Answer Text :
"P4081581417" "Maybe I am. But today, I won, and you lost."
// Answer Text :
"P264767485" "I'm nothing like you, Duncan. One day, I'll make sure you don't get away."
// Page Won Text :
"P2187153131" "<color orange>Praetor Duncan laughs, putting a hand to her chest.</color><br><br>For today, {HeroName}. Just for today. I'll be interested in seeing where you go from here. Maybe you'll become a Praetor one day, or maybe you'll even become more powerful than Marcus himself. Though, that would require something... <i>extraordinary</i>, given Marcus' whole little <color yellow>Incarnate</color> powers. But you should know this, {HeroName}.<br><br>When I get the chance, when you don't have Praetor White and the public on your side, I <i>will</i> make my move to kill you."
// Answer Text :
"P1604820873" "I'll be ready, trust me. Pleasure talking with you, Duncan."
// Page GetAway Text :
"P4148696959" "Oh, tough words, {HeroName}, tough words! Maybe you're under the delusion that what you're doing is all <i>good</i>, is that it? A little person who makes {Hero.gender=male his|her} own crimes to look good cleaning them up?<br><br>Let's just say this, {HeroName}. I'll be looking forward to the day that you try to put me down for good. Because on that day, I'll make sure you're killed, just like all the other trash here in Praetoria."
// Answer Text :
"P2005302554" "I wouldn't count on that, Duncan. Goodbye, for now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - CalvinScott 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1324275992" "{HeroName}, everyone is buzzing here about your efforts on the topside. We heard you're about to eliminate the Destroyers! Believe me, none of us here have any love for them. This is a win/win situation for all of us. If everything goes according to plan, we'll also have Praetor Duncan out of our hair as well! You're doing a terrific job, believe me. I couldn't have planned this better myself.<br><br>Is there anything you wished to discuss? If not, we need to go back to radio silence."
// Answer Text :
"P789206692" "Nothing, I'll be on my way."
// Answer Text :
"P526664090" "Have you been tracking Stern?"
// Answer Text :
"P3663108590" "Has anything happened with Aria?"
// Answer Text :
"P1559486951" "Has Zane done anything of note?"
// Page Stern Text :
"P265266127" "From what I've seen, Stern has gone in to have several of his cybernetics upgraded. It seems someone in the PPD is intending to prepare him for something; what exactly that is I'm unsure of. We're all prepared for the worst down here."
// Answer Text :
"P270063350" "Alright, I'll be on my way."
// Page Aria Text :
"P3803654623" "Aria is doing some secret work for Praetor Sinclair, it seems. I'm not sure what she's up to, but she has appeared several times in the same area as Sinclair, then she tried to attack us down in the tunnels. My guess would be that Praetor Sinclair is recruiting help from Powers Division. It can only mean that various plans of ours are about to see the light of day."
// Answer Text :
"P2427428480" "I'll be on my way."
// Page Zane Text :
"P2151608303" "We've seen Zane going back and forth in People's Park. I would guess that he's doing some training of a sort. He's also visited Cole Memorial Hospital in Nova Praetoria. If I could guess, I would say that he's visiting a family member in there, but we can't know for sure."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3705755238" "Things are escalating very quickly, {HeroName}. It's all becoming <i>very</i> exciting, I have to tell you! So, I've arranged for a full report to be given to TPN about the Destroyers. But, um, so I think Duncan is well aware of what we would plan to do with this information. Well, to be specific, she's aware of what <i>someone</i> is going to do with this information. She isn't aware of <i>who</i> has it. Or, uhm, maybe she is. I don't know. But I'm betting that she isn't gonna be able to make a move directly on you, given you're basically in with Praetor White.<br><br>Point being is that from what Mr. G has told me, <color yellow>there is a horde of one hundred Destroyers making their way to TPN through the tunnels</color>. They're looking to take down TPN before the news can get out about Praetor Duncan! But see, {HeroName}, this is PERFECT! I've got everything set up for you!"
// AcceptString :
"P472755992" "How is this perfect, exactly?"
// SendOffString :
"P4073338332" "First off, here, you can use these.<br><br><color orange>Tami hands you a bag of... grenades?</color><br><br>Secondly, what's happening right now is that <color orange>TPN is preparing to film you holding off the Destroyer horde</color>. This is going to be HUGE, {HeroName}. This'll go down in the history of Praetoria, no one will ever forget this! You'll need to get to the TPN campus right away and get yourself ready for a fight!<br><br><color Paragon>Members of the Resistance working undercover for Calvin Scott should inform him of what is happening.</color>"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P1039701439" "<color deepskyblue>Part Four: Destroyer Stand Off</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2256997212" "Defend TPN from the Destroyer Horde"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P886071390" "I'll be waiting eagerly, {HeroName}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P572752749" "It looks like there are some Destroyers already on the scene. You'll have to hurry to get things started."

