// Dialog :
"P3042605838" "You've handled the Destroyers last push to kill you and destroy TPN. Time to settle things with Praetor Duncan."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2270111720" "Meet with Praetor Duncan"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3155787252" "The report on TPN was huge, {HeroName}, huge! Now it's just time to settle things with Praetor Duncan, then we can call it a day!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4177358398" "You've finished things with Praetor Duncan."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskBegin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1565915475" "You receive a bag of grenades to help deal with the Destroyer horde."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P721457059" "This was all simply amazing, {HeroName}, simple amazing. TPN is running videos of you fighting the Destroyers non-stop. John Houston is giving commentary on the various moves you pulled off in the battle, and the people of Imperial City believe you to be an unstoppable force that they can all rely on. All in all, I say things turned out for the best! The Destroyers still linger in Nova and Imperial, but without their main stash of Fixadine, they will eventually die out. They're certaintly not going to become any more powerful than they currently are.<br><br>All of this has gotten the attention of Praetor Sinclair. You see, he's in a bit of, um, a bit of a jam. And given how you took Praetor Duncan down a few pegs, he's requested that I send you to meet him right away."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
